00:25:16,948 --> 00:25:19,048
The result is...

479
00:25:19,548 --> 00:25:20,748
On the right side of the chart.

480
00:25:20,848 --> 00:25:24,548
But when you have these point of controls at the same level, you have a ratio up here.

481
00:25:25,048 --> 00:25:26,704
Again, the point of control is

482
00:25:26,704 --> 00:25:28,912
you came back up towards the ratio and

483
00:25:28,912 --> 00:25:31,948
you couldn't get up to that level or get past it.

484
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:34,148
And then the market sells off.

485
00:25:34,148 --> 00:25:39,648
But your first starting point as the resistance level is where all these point of controls are.

486
00:25:41,048 --> 00:25:44,348
Your second part is up here at the top where you have the ratio.

487
00:25:44,348 --> 00:25:51,648
So anywhere between this high and these point of controls is going to be your area of resistance.

488
00:25:51,648 --> 00:25:53,348
I said it's a resistance area.

489
00:25:53,448 --> 00:25:55,409
People get blinded and think it's

490
00:25:55,409 --> 00:25:58,024
going to be a single price like you

491
00:25:58,024 --> 00:26:01,947
think, oh, this is your resistance, and we're on the other side.

492
00:26:02,348 --> 00:26:05,148
by a few ticks that it's not going to hold well.

493
00:26:06,848 --> 00:26:10,748
I think it's poor thinking, poor analysis in that respect.

494
00:26:11,348 --> 00:26:12,495
I said it's an

495
00:26:12,495 --> 00:26:14,216
area, and we came back into

496
00:26:14,216 --> 00:26:15,937
the area, and we rejected the

497
00:26:15,937 --> 00:26:17,945
prices up here, and we sold off.

498
00:26:21,448 --> 00:26:24,748
Again, you've got the selling imbalance.

499
00:26:24,848 --> 00:26:26,185
We spend a lot of time

500
00:26:26,185 --> 00:26:27,522
below it. We do come back

501
00:26:27,522 --> 00:26:29,304
up into it. We trade just on the

502
00:26:29,304 --> 00:26:32,646
other side, just on the other side of the point of control and continue lower.

503
00:26:33,248 --> 00:26:35,057
Now, for me, I prefer

504
00:26:35,057 --> 00:26:37,590
to use this selling imbalance, have this

505
00:26:37,590 --> 00:26:40,847
zone drawn out. I draw it out five spaces.

506
00:26:41,248 --> 00:26:44,548
I'm not looking for it to hold the rest of the day.

507
00:26:45,748 --> 00:26:52,848
Using it as an immediate support or resistance level, depending on what type of stacked imbalance you have it.

508
00:26:52,848 --> 00:27:00,648
But if after five bars, I really feel it loses its effectiveness.

509
00:27:00,848 --> 00:27:04,748
In this case, it did come back in the eighth bar and tested it and held again.

510
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:08,348
But for the most part, I'm really looking forward to hold over the next five bars.

511
00:27:08,948 --> 00:27:14,948
For me, I like the move to happen fairly quick rather than wait out to...

512
00:27:15,448 --> 00:27:18,848
You know, wait out 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 bars.

513
00:27:19,548 --> 00:27:20,529
But you see, I

514
00:27:20,529 --> 00:27:22,001
mean, the same analysis, you know,

515
00:27:22,001 --> 00:27:23,473
this is your initial zone, you

516
00:27:23,473 --> 00:27:27,645
know, then you'll be looking at the point of control, you know, in worst case up here.

517
00:27:27,648 --> 00:27:32,048
So, you know, this bar is going to be your resistance, you know, you can't

518
00:27:32,048 --> 00:27:36,348
came back up into resistance, got back through it a little bit, and then sold off.

519
00:27:36,548 --> 00:27:37,483
You know, I mean,

520
00:27:37,483 --> 00:27:39,354
once you start trading on the other side

521
00:27:39,354 --> 00:27:41,225
of this zone, okay, you could start to,

522
00:27:41,225 --> 00:27:43,096
I don't want to say worry, but, you

523
00:27:43,096 --> 00:27:43,797
know, you start

524
00:27:43,797 --> 00:27:45,434
to really pay attention and, you know,

525
00:27:45,434 --> 00:27:49,644
see how price is acting as you get to the point of control or up near the high.

