00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:09,227
at 850, we've broken out of this area, point of control is much higher.

561
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:16,008
But you're going to be looking now as this point of control here at 1903 as your support area.

562
00:30:16,108 --> 00:30:18,204
And if you could be getting along somewhere

563
00:30:18,204 --> 00:30:20,038
in there, it didn't pull back as

564
00:30:20,038 --> 00:30:23,444
much as you'd like. It only got down to 1904, but it continued higher.

565
00:30:28,408 --> 00:30:31,308
Okay, you know, this is a 15-minute chart, and...

566
00:30:34,208 --> 00:30:37,308
15-minute charts are time-based charts.

567
00:30:38,708 --> 00:30:40,780
Usually I look at range charts,

568
00:30:40,780 --> 00:30:42,852
but I threw this up here

569
00:30:42,852 --> 00:30:46,306
because it's one of those things that's important to note.

570
00:30:48,508 --> 00:30:53,608
Whether you trade a time-based chart or a range-based chart, you still want to analyze the same things.

571
00:30:54,008 --> 00:30:55,408
So the market is working its

572
00:30:55,408 --> 00:30:56,808
way down, working its way down,

573
00:30:56,808 --> 00:30:58,908
and then all of a sudden you get this.

574
00:30:59,408 --> 00:31:02,708
15 minute chart, right? So you get four point of controls right at the same level.

575
00:31:03,608 --> 00:31:04,089
Okay, and

